'' linux-arm64: cva_list is AAPCS64's std::__va_list, 'St9__va_list' -- a third spelling beside
'' Windows/Darwin's 'Pc' and x86-64 Linux's 'A1_13__va_list_tag'. And fbc's substitution rule
'' for it: the type itself is NEVER written as S<n>_ but EVERY occurrence is a candidate, while
'' a reference or pointer to it is an ordinary candidate. Every line below is fbc's own symbol,
'' measured with fbc-modern -target linux-aarch64 -r and fbc 1.10.1 native in the Lima VM
'' (2026-11-19, docs/tiko-linux-arm64 probes/l1-fbc). clang++ would write R as ...S0_.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target linux-arm64 --emit-ir tests/codegen/src/cva-list-mangle.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: @"_ZN1N1PERSt9__va_list"(
'' EXPECT-OUT: @"_ZN1N1QERSt9__va_listS1_"(
'' EXPECT-OUT: @"_ZN1N1RESt9__va_listSt9__va_list"(
'' EXPECT-OUT: @"_ZN1N1SESt9__va_listRSt9__va_list"(
'' EXPECT-OUT: @"_ZN1N1TERSt9__va_listSt9__va_list"(
'' EXPECT-OUT: @"_ZN1N1UESt9__va_listSt9__va_listRSt9__va_listS3_"(
'' EXPECT-OUT: @"_ZN1N1VEPSt9__va_listSt9__va_list"(
'' EXPECT-OUT: @"_ZN1N1WEPSt9__va_listS1_"(
